"""Build a browser-local workbench; no BINs or live transmit code are deployed."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def build(shell,write):
    report=json.loads((ROOT/'analysis/firmware/decode_catalog.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
    for image in report['images']:
        maps=json.loads((ROOT/image['maps_path']).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
        keys=('id','display_name','data_address','end_exclusive','rows','columns','element_bytes','byte_order','kind','row_axis','column_axis','input_min_raw','index_divisor','index_factor_raw')
        write('tools/maps/'+image['id']+'.json',json.dumps([{k:m[k] for k in keys if k in m} for m in maps],ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
    body='''<div class="page-heading"><div class="kicker">XT660 / WORKBENCH</div><h1>Back up. Inspect. Develop.</h1><p>Local BIN tools and serial receive capture. Files stay in your browser; nothing is uploaded.</p></div>
<nav class="tool-links" aria-label="Workbench sections"><a href="#backup">BIN &amp; backup</a><a href="#tune">Map editor</a><a href="#connect">COM capture</a><a href="#protocol">Protocol</a></nav>
<p id="tool-error" class="notice" role="alert" hidden></p>
<section id="backup" class="tool-panel"><h2>Open a BIN</h2><p>Identify an existing file, keep an untouched copy and compare two reads. A local file is not proof of a complete ECU backup: boot and persistent storage need separate coverage.</p><label class="file-label">BIN file<input id="bin-file" type="file" accept=".bin,application/octet-stream"></label><p id="bin-status" role="status">No file opened.</p><dl id="bin-facts" class="firmware-facts"></dl>
<div class="tool-actions"><button id="backup-save" disabled>Save untouched BIN</button><button id="backup-report" disabled>Save identity report</button></div>
<label class="file-label">Compare another read<input id="compare-file" type="file" disabled></label><p id="compare-status" role="status"></p></section>
<section id="tune" class="tool-panel"><h2>Raw-map editor</h2><p>Editing is available only for an exact registered BIN hash. Values are raw integers; physical scaling is unfinished. The loaded file determines the map layout, independently of the bike selector.</p>
<label>Map<select id="tune-map" disabled><option>Open a registered BIN first</option></select></label><p id="tune-status" role="status"></p><div id="tune-grid" class="tune-scroll"></div>
<form id="tune-form"><p id="cell-info">Select a cell to edit.</p><label>Raw value<input id="cell-value" type="number" min="0" step="1" disabled required></label><button id="cell-apply" disabled>Apply to draft</button></form>
<div class="tool-actions"><button id="edit-undo" disabled>Undo last edit</button><button id="edit-reset" disabled>Discard edits</button><button id="draft-save" disabled>Save draft BIN</button><button id="draft-report" disabled>Save change report</button></div>
<p id="edit-status" role="status">The original file is kept unchanged in memory. Draft export does not repair checksums or make a flash-ready file.</p></section>
<section id="connect" class="tool-panel"><h2>COM-port receive capture</h2><p>Select a serial adapter using the browser’s port picker. This version records received bytes only; it does not request a memory dump or send commands. Use an ECU-compatible electrical interface, not bare USB-UART wiring to a vehicle signal.</p>
<label>Baud rate<input id="serial-baud" type="number" min="300" max="1000000" step="1" placeholder="Enter your interface baud rate" required></label><p class="tool-note">8 data bits · no parity · 1 stop bit. The application tool requests 15,625 baud. Boot SCI0 has a different divisor (about 9,615 baud at the nominal clock); its wiring and clock still need bench confirmation. Opening a port can change adapter control-line states.</p>
<div class="tool-actions"><button id="serial-connect">Choose COM port &amp; receive</button><button id="serial-stop" disabled>Disconnect</button><button id="serial-save" disabled>Save RX capture</button></div><p id="serial-status" role="status">Disconnected. Desktop browser support for Web Serial is required.</p><pre id="serial-log" aria-label="Received serial bytes"></pre><p>Capture stops at 2 MiB. USB chunk boundaries are not ECU packet boundaries. Starting a new connection replaces the previous capture.</p></section>
<section id="protocol" class="tool-panel"><h2>Understand the bytes</h2><p>Inspect an explicitly delimited frame from a capture. A matching checksum alone does not prove which protocol the ECU is speaking.</p><label>Frame type<select id="frame-type"><option value="boot">Recovered boot frame</option><option value="application">Application five-byte reply</option></select></label><label>Hexadecimal bytes<textarea id="frame-bytes" rows="3" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste one complete frame"></textarea></label><button id="frame-decode">Decode frame</button><pre id="frame-result"></pre>
<details><summary>Read-command preview — offline only</summary><p>The recovered boot uses command 03 with a 16-bit address. This preview is derived from static code. It does not open a session or transmit anything.</p><label>CPU address (hex)<input id="read-address" value="1800" pattern="[0-9A-Fa-f]{1,4}"></label><label>Bytes to read<select id="read-mode"><option value="0">2</option><option value="1">16</option><option value="2">512</option><option value="3">2048</option><option value="4">256</option><option value="5">1024</option></select></label><button id="read-preview">Show request bytes</button><pre id="read-result"></pre></details>
<h3>ECU readout &amp; flashing</h3><p>The boot contains read, staging, erase and programming handlers. Live dumping and flashing remain unavailable until the SCI0 electrical route, entry/session sequence, timing and recovery are validated on the target hardware. The Yamaha service-tool KWP sequence is comparison evidence, not a drop-in XT boot driver.</p><a href="../docs/firmware/FLASH_TOOLING.html">Protocol evidence, tool findings and what remains ↗</a></section>'''
    write('tools/index.html',shell('Tools — backup, maps and serial capture',body,'tools/index.html','Tools','<link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/tools.css"><script type="module" src="../assets/tools.mjs"></script>'))
